---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.5 · Quest Cleanup, Dragon Slayer II & Desert Treasure II" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-5" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Quest Cleanup, Dragon Slayer II &amp; Desert Treasure II</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Close the remaining Quest Cape loose ends, take the last Runecraft level only when it is needed, and finish both old Grandmasters with the gear this route actually owns.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Quest Cape cleanup and DT2 prerequisite chains → Dragon Slayer II → live Runecraft remainder to 60 → Desert Treasure II → carry the live skill tab into the final chapter."
        stats={["Actual 60 Runecraft, plus a live 71-Woodcutting check at Grim Tales", "75+ Magic and Ranged, 74+ Slayer, Fire Cape and 70+ Crafting carry in", "Dragon Slayer II gives 80,000 Smithing XP before the later Blood Moon Rises check"]}
        unlocks={["Contact!, Beneath Cursed Sands, Secrets of the North and the DT2 miniquests", "Myths' Guild, Ring of shadows and Scar essence access", "No Bowfa, blowpipe, RCB drop, Slayer helmet, trident or Ava's assembler requirement"]}
      />
      <div class="callout"><strong>Quest journal first.</strong> This page closes quests the mandatory route had not actually checked off, not every optional activity a returning player may have sampled. A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest were completed in 3.3. Learning the Ropes is Tutorial Island, already completed before Chapter 1. If your journal already shows any cleanup quest green, skip its work; still check that every named quest is green before attempting a Quest Cape.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest Cape cleanup · currently released quests</div><h2>Close the old loose ends before the Grandmasters.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-prince-ali" number="1" title="Complete Prince Ali Rescue">
        <p>This easy classic was never scheduled earlier. Start with <strong>Hassan in Al Kharid Palace</strong>, then work with Osman and Leela around Al Kharid/Draynor to disguise the prince and get him past the jail guard. Before leaving, stage <strong>one soft clay, three balls of wool, one yellow dye, one redberries, one ashes, one bucket of water, one pot of flour, one bronze bar, one pink skirt, three beers, one rope and 100 coins</strong>. Bank between disguise and rescue phases. The reason to do it <em>now</em> is concrete: <strong>Contact! requires it</strong>. Do not retrofit it into Chapter 1. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Prince_Ali_Rescue" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Buy and make the prince's disguise before the jail trip" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Draynor/Port Sarim:</strong> buy the rope from <strong>Ned</strong>; give him <strong>three balls of wool</strong> for the wig. If wool is absent, shear three sheep at Lumbridge and spin the wool at the castle wheel. Buy a yellow dye from <strong>Oronwen in Lletya</strong>, or give <strong>Aggie in Draynor two onions and five coins</strong>; onions grow in the field north of Rimmington. Buy <strong>one redberries and one pot of flour from Wydin in Port Sarim</strong>.</p>
          <p><strong>Varrock/Lumbridge:</strong> buy the <strong>pink skirt from Thessalia in Varrock</strong> and <strong>three ordinary beers from a pub</strong>; keep the beers full for Joe. Mine one clay at the south-west Varrock mine and add water for soft clay. Mine one copper and one tin at Lumbridge Swamp and smelt the bronze bar. Burn one normal log and pick up its ashes; refill a bucket with water for the skin paste.</p>
          <p>Keep <strong>100 coins after shopping</strong> for the quest/travel allowance. The clay makes the key impression, the bronze bar becomes the key through Osman, and Aggie makes the skin paste from the food/ash/water ingredients. These are fresh quest consumables; earlier dye, wool and bar purchases are not assumed still banked. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Prince_Ali_Rescue/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Complete ingredient checklist</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-classic-cleanup" number="2" title="Clear the remaining classic Quest Cape entries">
        <p>Check the journal, then finish <strong>The Corsair Curse, Scorpion Catcher, Spirits of the Elid, Ratcatchers, Rag and Bone Man I, Rag and Bone Man II, Olaf's Quest and Grim Tales</strong> if they are still red. They were absent or explicitly deferred in the mandatory route; none requires redesigning Chapters 1–2. Quest Helper may handle dialogue, but do the long item/bone collection in sensible trips rather than carrying every quest's kit at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Preparation check:</strong> Spirits of the Elid needs a bow plus arrows, a normal needle/two thread and three melee damage styles; Ratcatchers needs its own cat/food/poison kit; Rag and Bone Man I/II use <strong>8 and 27 special bones</strong> with fresh vinegar/logs. For Grim Tales, verify <strong>71 Woodcutting</strong> before the quest and reserve <strong>two tarromin potions (unf)</strong>. Use the grouped notes for exact suppliers and local replacements.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Corsair Curse, Scorpion Catcher and Spirits of the Elid" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>The Corsair Curse:</strong> bank food and ordinary combat gear before the boat from Rimmington. The quest supplies its investigation tools: take the <strong>tinderbox near Gnocci upstairs</strong> and the <strong>spade on the south side of Corsair Cove</strong> when needed. Its bank opens after completion, so do not count it as a mid-quest supply stop.</p>
          <p><strong>Scorpion Catcher:</strong> Thormac at the Sorcerer's Tower gives the scorpion cage. With the route's <strong>70 Agility</strong>, use Taverley Dungeon's pipe shortcut instead of fetching another dusty key; take dragonfire protection for the adult-dragon area. The barcrawl and monastery Prayer access are already covered. A missing anti-dragon shield can be replaced through Duke Horacio in Lumbridge.</p>
          <p><strong>Spirits of the Elid:</strong> carry <strong>one air rune, one law rune, one normal needle, two thread, knife, rope, pickaxe and a lit light source</strong>, plus food/desert supplies. Buy needle/thread from Dommik, rope from Ned and the two runes from an unlocked rune shop. Be on the <strong>standard spellbook</strong> for Telekinetic Grab. A costume needle does not repair these robes.</p>
          <p>Take the dragon scimitar for <strong>slash</strong> and the Heroes' Guild dragon mace for <strong>stab and crush</strong>, selecting the actual attack styles for the golems. The water-channel target needs a <strong>bow and arrows</strong>; a crossbow does not work. Take the quest's <strong>shortbow east of the cave entrance and bronze arrows south of it</strong> if your old bow is missing. The torn robes and ancestral key are obtained in Nardah during the investigation. Retain the shortbow for DS2's Barbarian Firemaking check. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Spirits_of_the_Elid/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Elid's full item and style requirements</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Ratcatchers: a usable cat, its food and the poison ingredients" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Bring a <strong>non-overgrown cat</strong>; an ordinary adult is much more reliable at catching rats than a kitten. If the cat was traded away, <strong>Gertrude sells a replacement kitten for 100 coins</strong>. Raise it during other cleanup quests if you want the adult's easier catching; purchasing a kitten does not instantly replace an adult. Reclaim a <strong>catspeak amulet from the Sphinx in Sophanem with your cat present</strong> if missing.</p>
          <p>Set aside <strong>four cheese, one bucket of milk, one clean marrentill, one unicorn horn dust, one pot of weeds, a tinderbox, a snake charm, 101 coins and about eight fish for the cat</strong>. Buy cheese from Wydin or the Culinaromancer's Chest, and milk from the chest or a dairy cow. Gerrant sells inexpensive raw fish. Use fish on the hole to heal the fighting cat; refill if its health demands more. The 101-coin allowance covers the snake-charmer sequence without relying on the ring-of-charos discount.</p>
          <p>Take <strong>one rat poison from the north-west branch of the Clock Tower basement</strong>; it is the same poison accepted here and avoids consuming a kwuarm. The crafting alternative is <strong>one clean kwuarm, one red spiders' eggs and one empty vial</strong> handed to Hooknosed Jack. For the separate cat-antipoison request, ordinary chaos druids in Taverley Dungeon can supply the missing <strong>marrentill</strong>; kill a unicorn near Lumbridge/Varrock for a horn and grind it. Make the pot of weeds by using raked weeds on an empty pot. Donate a coin to <strong>Ali the Snake Charmer in Pollnivneach</strong> for a missing charm. Stop herb gathering at the actual one-herb deficit. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ratcatchers/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cat, poison and fish checklist</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Rag and Bone Man I/II: vinegar, special bones and the missing Mogre unlock" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Start each bone list before collecting its drops.</strong> For I, gather its <strong>eight special bones</strong> from a goblin, monkey, bear, unicorn, giant rat, giant bat, ram and big frog. Ordinary bones do not substitute. Goblins, rats, rams, bears and unicorns are available around Lumbridge/Varrock; use Karamja for a monkey and a giant bat in the volcano dungeon, and Lumbridge Swamp/Caves for the big frog.</p>
          <p><strong>Processing stock:</strong> I needs <strong>eight empty pots, eight normal logs, a tinderbox and eight jugs of vinegar</strong>. Buy pots from a general store, cut the logs, then ask <strong>Fortunato in Draynor</strong> about vinegar and buy it for one coin per jug. Add vinegar to pots, add each special bone, and boil it on the Odd Old Man's pot-boiler with a log. Keep the pots. II uses <strong>27 special bones, 27 fresh jugs of vinegar and 27 fresh normal logs</strong>; prepare 27 pots if filling everything at the bank, or reuse I's pots in smaller batches. Those are separate consumptions after I, not its eight vinegar/logs counted again.</p>
          <p><strong>Before the Mogre bone:</strong> finish <strong>Skippy and the Mogres</strong> at Mudskipper Point if still incomplete. Bring <strong>one bucket of water, one nettle tea, one bucket of milk, one chocolate dust and one snape grass</strong>. Pick <strong>nettles beside Edgeville's yew trees</strong> while wearing gloves, add them to a bowl of water and cook it for the tea. Buy chocolate and milk from the Culinaromancer's Chest, grind the chocolate, add it to the milk and then add the snape grass for the hangover cure. Collect this <strong>one extra snape grass</strong> from the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>repeatable ground-spawn source</a>; do not take it out of an already-counted Prayer-potion batch.</p>
          <p><strong>II's hunting kit:</strong> take a lit enclosed light and tinderbox, axe, Ranged weapon with ammunition for vultures, and a <strong>mirror shield or the retained V's shield</strong> for basilisks. Buy an initial <strong>ten ice coolers and ten fishing explosives from a Slayer equipment shop</strong>; replace them if the relevant bone has not dropped before they run out. Keep <strong>902 coins</strong> for 27 vinegar and the 875-coin Brimhaven Dungeon entry, plus any chosen travel fares. A dusty key is unnecessary with 70 Agility; bring a rope only if using an unroped Lumbridge Swamp entrance.</p>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>II collection trip</th><th>Required special-bone sources</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Morytania</td><td>Bat south of the Odd Old Man; undead cow west of the Ectofuntus; experiment beneath Fenkenstrain's graveyard; werewolf in Canifis (do not use Wolfbane); ghoul west of Canifis.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Varrock / Lumbridge</td><td>Ordinary rat and zombie in Varrock Sewers; cave goblin in the eastern Lumbridge caves. A giant rat does not give II's rat bone.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Desert</td><td>Jackal, desert snake and desert lizard north of Nardah; vulture south-west of Nardah. Finish the lizard with an ice cooler and range the vulture.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Port Sarim</td><td>Seagull on the docks; ice giant in the Asgarnian Ice Dungeon; Mogre at Mudskipper Point, summoned with a fishing explosive after Skippy.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Karamja / Taverley</td><td>Jogre on Karamja; moss giant and fire giant in Brimhaven Dungeon; baby blue dragon in Taverley Dungeon.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Fremennik area</td><td>Troll in the cave by Keldagrim's entrance; rabbit south-east of Rellekka; basilisk in Fremennik Slayer Dungeon; dagannoth in Waterbirth's first dungeon room.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Gnome / Feldip</td><td>Terrorbird in the Tree Gnome Stronghold; wolf and ogre in Feldip Hills; Zogre in Jiggig.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>Keep killing each eligible creature only until its <strong>specific quest bone</strong> is obtained; there is no fixed kill-count guarantee. Read the in-game bone list to check what is already stored or handed in before repeating trips. Bank by region, then do the vinegar/boiling batch. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rag_and_Bone_Man_II/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Bone and equipment checklist</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Skippy_and_the_Mogres/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Skippy's ingredients</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <ExpandableNote title="Olaf's Quest and Grim Tales" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Olaf's Quest:</strong> take an <strong>axe, tinderbox and spade</strong>, plus food/combat supplies. Bob in Lumbridge sells a basic axe and general stores sell the other two. Collect the quest's wood and dungeon materials as directed; no earlier cold-weather supply stock is assumed.</p>
          <p><strong>Grim Tales:</strong> inspect actual Woodcutting. The earlier route guarantees 70, while the quest checks <strong>71 Woodcutting</strong> (boostable). If short and using no boost, train just the remaining level with ordinary maples, yews or familiar Sulliusceps, then stop at 71. Its <strong>60,000 Woodcutting XP</strong> arrives after the quest and cannot fund entry; apply it before Chapter 3.6's later 74 target.</p>
          <p>Bring <strong>two tarromin potions (unf)</strong>, an axe, seed dibber, <strong>filled watering can</strong> and food. If the two unfinished potions are missing, obtain two tarromin from ordinary chaos druids, clean them and mix each with a vial of water bought from Jatix; keep both unfinished for the shrinking potion. Withdraw the farming tools from a leprechaun or buy them from Sarah south of Falador. Recover the <strong>door key from the pot outside the Witch's House in Taverley</strong>. The ogleroots, beans and other story materials come from the quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Grim_Tales/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Grim Tales preparation</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-varlamore-cleanup" number="3" title="Finish the currently released Varlamore and Lumbridge loose ends">
        <p>Complete <strong>The Ides of Milk</strong> (start with Cassius by Lumbridge pond), then <strong>The Ribbiting Tale of a Lily Pad Labour Dispute</strong> (Marcellus at Locus Oasis; bring an axe), <strong>Meat and Greet</strong> (Emelio in Outer Fortis), <strong>At First Light</strong> (Guildmaster Apatura at the Hunter Guild; Eagles' Peak is already done; bring a needle, hammer and a box trap or two jerboa tails), and <strong>Shadows of Custodia</strong> (read the Auburn Pub notice board; bring four <strong>finished, strung willow longbows</strong>, four maple logs, a hammer, a fishing rod and combat food). <strong>If you completed Ribbiting Tale for the optional hardwood patch in 1.4, skip that quest here and finish the remaining cleanup entries.</strong> The route already exceeds the latter quests' skill checks. These are Quest Cape completions, not requirements for Jad or a new gear farm. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quests/List" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest list</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Small local supplies for each cleanup quest" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>The Ides of Milk and Meat and Greet</strong> supply their investigation items during the quests; no outside milk, meat or seed collection is required. For <strong>The Ribbiting Tale</strong>, take the axe from the logs beside Marcellus if your banked axe is not with you. If the quest is already green, do not count its XP a second time.</p>
          <p><strong>At First Light:</strong> bring one box trap or two embertailed jerboa tails. <strong>Imia on the north side of the Hunter Guild's surface sells a box trap for 41 coins</strong>; catch the two jerboas near the Locus Oasis during the quest. A needle spawns in the <strong>south-east surface corner of the Hunter Guild</strong>, and a hammer in the <strong>house north of Atza</strong>. The leaves, fur and toy are supplied in the story. Keep the second tail for the cat bed.</p>
          <p><strong>Shadows of Custodia:</strong> buy <strong>four finished willow longbows from Arcuani's Archery Supplies in Tal Teklan</strong>, as in the current BRUHsailer preparation. If making them instead, cut four willow logs, knife four willow longbows (u) and attach four bow strings at 40 Fletching; the strings can be spun from four flax. Cut <strong>four maple logs near Seers' Village</strong>, buy a fishing rod from Gerrant and a hammer from a general store if missing. Unstrung bows and maple planks do not fill these handoffs. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Shadows_of_Custodia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Custodia's item list</a>.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-contact" number="4" title="Complete Contact! immediately after Prince Ali Rescue">
        <p><strong>Icthlarin's Little Helper and Gertrude's Cat</strong> are already complete. Speak to the High Priest in Sophanem. Bring a reliable, preferably non-extinguishable light source, a tinderbox backup, antipoison, food, Prayer restores and an exit teleport. The Scabarite dungeon is the awkward part: traps can extinguish ordinary lights, so do not enter with only an unrelightable option. For the level-191 Giant Scarab, use the route's ranged/magic kit, maintain the relevant protection prayer and keep enough food to survive mistakes. Claim <strong>7,000 Thieving XP, Keris and Sophanem bank/shop access</strong>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Replace the light and refill before the Scabarite dungeon" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Reuse the <strong>lit sapphire/bullseye lantern</strong> from WGS, keeping a tinderbox. If the lantern is missing, follow the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-wgs`}>lantern recovery recipe</a>. Bank before entering the dungeon, and make missing <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions and antipoison</a>. Ordinary stat restores do not replace those Prayer doses; leave room for food and quest items.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>The combat reward is <strong>one bankable lamp with two separate 7,000-XP choices</strong> from Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic—not two lamps and not a Slayer option. With actual 75 Magic already solved, put both choices into <strong>Strength by default</strong> unless the live account has a better immediate combat need. Record two allocations from the one reward, exactly once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Contact!" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Contact! mechanics</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-beneath-sands" number="5" title="Complete Beneath Cursed Sands">
        <p>Do this after Contact!. Its actual <strong>62 Agility, 55 Crafting and 55 Firemaking</strong> checks are already cleared. Start with <strong>Jamila at her Sophanem stall</strong>, then meet Maisa; bank-check a <strong>one coal, one iron bar, tinderbox, spade and one raw beef</strong> before the multi-area trip. Bring desert heat protection, food, restores, antipoison and the normal melee/ranged switches. The Head Menaphite Guard punishes active protection prayers, so bring real food and turn overheads off for that fight. Kite the Champion of Scabaras with Ranged and <strong>Protect from Magic</strong>, and re-bank for the later Menaphite Akh/scarab-mage fights as needed. Claim <strong>50,000 Agility XP</strong> and the <strong>Keris partisan</strong>. Tombs of Amascut access is a useful unlock, but completing the raid is optional post-guide content. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Beneath_Cursed_Sands" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="One metal bar and one accepted meat" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy <strong>one raw beef from Wydin in Port Sarim</strong> or kill a Lumbridge cow and keep its meat raw for the quest. Fish does not fill this request. Mine <strong>one coal</strong> at a coal rock, and mine/smelt iron ore until <strong>one iron bar</strong> succeeds if the bank has none. The normal Blast Furnace Ore Seller is an alternative for missing ore.</p>
          <p>Buy a missing spade/tinderbox from a general store. Fill waterskins at a water source before the desert trip and bank by phase; do not consume the reserved raw beef as part of your food plan. Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer, stat restore and antipoison supplies</a> against the actual remaining bank.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Mahjarrat chain · mandatory miniquests only</div><h2>Connect the actual DT2 prerequisites.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-enakhra" number="6" title="Complete Enakhra's Lament on the standard spellbook">
        <p>Start with Lazim just north-east of the Desert Quarry. The checks are <strong>50 Crafting and 43 Prayer, not boostable; 39 Magic and the listed 45 Firemaking check are boostable</strong> (the Firemaking level helps identify brazier fuel rather than preventing trial-and-error). The route exceeds them. Stage a kit, banking between phases if necessary: <strong>chisel, tinderbox, ordinary candle, normal/oak/willow/maple logs, a whole acceptable food item for Pentyn, soft clay, coal and pickaxe</strong>; bring a water container if making the clay onsite. Mine <strong>52 kg of sandstone and two 5 kg granite pieces</strong> at the quarry if not banked. Use standard-book runes for a wind bolt/blast/wave or better, a fire bolt/blast/wave or better, and <strong>Crumble Undead</strong> (bring spare casts); keep enough Prayer for a short Protect from Melee use. Desert heat supplies and a teleport make the trip less brittle. Claim the fixed <strong>7,000 XP each in Crafting, Mining, Firemaking and Magic</strong>, then read live levels without projecting extra gates. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Enakhra%27s_Lament/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">One-trip item reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Accepted food, ordinary fuel and actual spell runes" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy <strong>one ordinary unlit candle from Catherby's candle maker</strong> and <strong>one whole bread from the Culinaromancer's Chest</strong> for Pentyn. Keep the bread uneaten; ordinary fish is not an accepted substitute. Cut <strong>one normal, one oak, one willow and one maple log</strong> for the braziers. Mine one clay and add water for <strong>one soft clay</strong>, and take <strong>one coal</strong> from the bank or a coal rock.</p>
          <p>Bring the pickaxe and chisel to the Desert Quarry. Mine a combined <strong>52 kg of sandstone</strong> and <strong>two intact 5 kg granite pieces</strong>; count the item sizes, not 52 sandstone items or two random granite pieces. Keep those pieces for Lazim and the temple, and bank excess mining output.</p>
          <p>On the <strong>standard spellbook</strong>, one Wind Bolt costs <strong>two air + one chaos</strong>, one Fire Bolt costs <strong>three air + four fire + one chaos</strong>, and one Crumble Undead costs <strong>two air + two earth + one chaos</strong>. A small ten-cast-per-spell starting pack is <strong>70 air, 40 fire, 20 earth and 30 chaos runes</strong>; bring spare casts for the actual fight and replace what is spent if retrying. Aubury in Varrock sells these runes. Strike spells are too weak for the bolt-or-better checks.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-empty-lord" number="7" title="Complete Curse of the Empty Lord and claim its museum lamp">
        <p>Use the <strong>ring of visibility</strong> from Desert Treasure I and a <strong>ghostspeak amulet</strong> to follow the current ghost sequence for all six pieces of <strong>Ghostly robes</strong>. Some stops are in the Wilderness. Bank valuables, take only replaceable travel/combat kit where needed, enable <strong>PK skull prevention</strong>, check your world and teleport limits, and never assume a quiet Wilderness is safe. On completion, show the full set to Historian Minas in the Varrock Museum for the <strong>10,000-XP antique lamp</strong> (skill level 50+). Put it in <strong>Fletching by default</strong> toward the later actual-70 Blood Moon Rises gate; do not silently treat it as having already reached that level. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Curse_of_the_Empty_Lord" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ghost route</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Recover the ghost-speaking kit and take a knife" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Reclaim a missing <strong>ring of visibility from Rasolo west of the Fishing Guild</strong> and a <strong>ghostspeak amulet from Father Urhney in Lumbridge Swamp</strong>. Take a <strong>knife</strong> from a general store as well; one assigned ghost route needs it. The quest supplies the six robe pieces as you visit its ghosts. Keep the complete set after showing Minas: The General's Shadow consumes access to that same outfit next.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-general-shadow" number="8" title="Complete The General's Shadow">
        <p>Full Ghostly robes, <strong>Fight Arena</strong> and the ring of visibility now cover the chain. Speak to the ghost of General Khazard south-east of Rellekka with the <strong>ghostspeak amulet, ring, all six robe pieces and at least 40 coins</strong>; use ordinary teleports for the scattered scouts. Bring ranged/magic combat kit and food for the level-160 <strong>Ghost of Bouncer</strong> in the Goblin Cave. <strong>Prayer cannot be used in that cave fight</strong>; safespot rather than relying on an overhead. Claim its fixed <strong>2,000 Slayer XP</strong> as incidental—the actual-74 Slayer gate was already closed in 3.4. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_General%27s_Shadow/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Scout and fight reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Keep all six Ghostly pieces together" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Bring <strong>all six Ghostly robe pieces, the ring of visibility, ghostspeak amulet and 40 coins</strong> together before speaking to Khazard. If a piece was lost, revisit the ghost who awarded it during Curse of the Empty Lord while wearing the ring/amulet; recover only the missing pieces. Do not treat the museum lamp as proof the outfit is still banked. Take real food for Bouncer because protection prayer is unavailable in his fight.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-secrets" number="9" title="Complete Secrets of the North; do not farm Phantom Muspah">
        <p>The hard <strong>69 Agility, 64 Thieving and 56 Hunter</strong> gates are already behind us. Check the journal for <strong>Making Friends with My Arm, The General's Shadow, Devious Minds and Hazeel Cult</strong>; only the General's Shadow branch was newly closed here. Start with the guard outside the Carnillean Mansion in East Ardougne. Bring <strong>100 coins and a normal lockpick</strong> (the Strange Old Lockpick does not work), plus a tinderbox, antipoison, food, Prayer restores and Weiss transport. Evelot, the Assassin and the Strange Creature are separate supply/combat phases: bank between them, move away from Assassin poison projectiles, and use the deterministic ranged/magic gear for the Strange Creature while learning its attack cycle. Claim <strong>60,000 Agility, 50,000 Thieving and 40,000 Hunter XP</strong>. The post-quest Phantom Muspah and its drops are optional. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Secrets_of_the_North" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="A normal lockpick and separate fight inventories" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Buy <strong>one normal lockpick from Martin Thwait in the Rogues' Den beneath Burthorpe's Toad and Chicken</strong> if none remains. The route already clears his 50-Agility/50-Thieving shop checks. Keep <strong>100 coins after shopping</strong>, a tinderbox and your Weiss travel method. Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>antipoison and Prayer potions</a> between the separate fights instead of assuming the last quest's doses remain.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-faithful" number="10" title="Complete His Faithful Servants, not a Barrows gear grind">
        <p>With Priest in Peril done, speak to the <strong>Strange Old Man at Barrows</strong> east of Mort'ton. Bring a <strong>spade</strong>, Barrows travel, Magic/combat gear, food and Prayer restores. Dig each of the six mounds and defeat its brother; one randomized mound leads to the tunnel instead, where the final brother appears on the way to the chest. Open that chest with <strong>at least six free inventory spaces</strong> so the strange icon is actually received; if a full inventory prevents the pickup, you may need to repeat the brothers. Then return it to the Old Man. No Barrows unique is needed. Claim the <strong>20,000 Prayer-XP lamp</strong>. This miniquest is mandatory specifically for DT2; other optional miniquests are not being pulled into the route. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/His_Faithful_Servants" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Miniquest reference</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="A spade, one Barrows run and six empty reward spaces" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>A general store sells the <strong>spade</strong> if your old one is missing. Bring your existing combat/Magic kit with actual runes or charges, food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions</a>. The <strong>strange icon is obtained from this miniquest's Barrows chest</strong>; it is not an item to farm elsewhere. Free six spaces before opening it and return the icon to the Strange Old Man.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Dragon Slayer II · before the final RC bridge</div><h2>Audit the bank, then take the first Grandmaster.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-ds2-preflight" number="11" title="Secure the Dragon Slayer II quest kit and live boss supplies">
        <p>Check <strong>200 quest points, actual 75 Magic, 70 Smithing, 68 Mining, 62 Crafting, 60 Agility, 60 Thieving, 50 Construction and 50 Hitpoints</strong> in the journal/skill tab. This route should clear them, but check live Hitpoints instead of inferring it from other combat levels. The direct prior quests are <strong>Legends' Quest, Dream Mentor, A Tail of Two Cats, Animal Magnetism, Ghosts Ahoy, Bone Voyage and Client of Kourend</strong>; check their own prerequisite chains in the journal rather than relying on a remembered quest-point total. Start with Alec Kincade outside the Myths' Guild after every required prior quest is green. Reserve a real food/restore/teleport/cash buffer; Chapter 3 has no guaranteed ending coin stack.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Manufacture the quest pieces and reserve their consumables" label="Quest preparation">
          <p><strong>Repairs:</strong> cut eight oak logs and take them to a sawmill with <strong>2,000 coins</strong> for eight oak planks. Buy <strong>ten swamp paste from a charter-ship Trader Crewmember</strong> such as Port Khazard's. Buy <strong>30 steel nails as a small starting buffer</strong> from a sawmill operator; the quest lists 12 required, with extras for breakage. Restock if that buffer is exhausted. These planks and nails are fresh stock after Brain Robbery.</p>
          <p><strong>Tools:</strong> a sawmill operator sells the saw, Jiminua near Tai Bwo Wannai sells a normal machete, Dommik sells a chisel, and general stores supply hammer/spade/tinderbox. Reuse the pickaxe and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/#i31-wgs`}>lit lantern and glassblowing pipe</a>; make <strong>two fresh molten glass from two sand and two soda ash</strong> at a furnace. Buy insulated boots from a Slayer equipment shop if missing.</p>
          <p><strong>Cat/ghost and Lunar access:</strong> the cat amulet must be <strong>enchanted, catspeak amulet (e)</strong>. If missing, take your cat to the Sphinx in Sophanem for the basic amulet, then bring it and <strong>five death runes to Hild in Burthorpe</strong> for enchantment. Father Urhney replaces ghostspeak amulets; Brundt replaces the seal of passage. Recover a missing anti-dragon shield from Duke Horacio before the dragon phases.</p>
          <p><strong>One goutweed:</strong> if Dream Mentor used the last one, steal another from the <strong>crates in the Troll Stronghold kitchen storeroom</strong>. A gout tuber is a different item; no gout-tuber or Farming grind is required. The cut dragonstone has its own recovery below and is reserved for this quest.</p>
          <p><strong>Runes:</strong> at 75 Magic, use <strong>three Fire Wave casts = 21 fire, 15 air and three blood runes</strong>, plus the separate <strong>one astral rune</strong>. Buy deficits from Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle. Keep the five death runes for Hild separate if re-enchanting the amulet. These small quest casts do not cover the boss-fight rune supply.</p>
          <p><strong>Barbarian Firemaking:</strong> cut <strong>one oak log</strong> for Otto's demonstration and use a normal bow on it; the initial training specifically uses oak, and the crossbow is not a fire-lighting bow. Reuse Spirits of the Elid's shortbow, or buy one from <strong>Lowe in Varrock</strong> if it was discarded. Ask about pyre ships afterward. For combat, refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer/antipoison/stat-restoration supplies</a> and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-3/#i33-ranged-kit`}>actual enchanted-bolt deficit</a> after Fight Caves and MM2.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Ancient Cavern access is a separate mandatory partial miniquest check.</strong> The Chapter 1 Barbarian Fishing foundation alone does not prove it. At Otto's Grotto, finish the first Barbarian Firemaking demonstration (light the taught fire with a bow), then ask Otto specifically about <strong>pyre ships</strong> so the whirlpool admits you to the Ancient Cavern for DS2's key-forging phase. You do <em>not</em> need to farm chewed bones or finish every Barbarian Training section. Bring a one-click teleport when first entering the dangerous cavern. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ancient_Cavern" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Access condition</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Bank audit:</strong> adamant crossbow (or already-owned RCB), <em>remaining</em> plain adamant, ruby (e) and diamond (e) bolts from 3.3, Ava's accumulator, anti-dragon shield, antifire doses, poison/venom cures, food, Prayer restores and optional run/restoration supplies. If antifire is missing, at the route's 69+ Herblore mix <strong>lantadyme + vial of water + dragon scale dust</strong> into three-dose antifire potions; collect blue dragon scales from the <strong>Taverley blue-dragon-area ground spawns</strong> through the 70-Agility shortcut and grind them with a pestle and mortar. Use anti-dragon protection near the dragons. Lantadyme from banked herbs/seeds or 60-Slayer aberrant spectres is <em>variable</em>: gather to the live number of doses needed for Vorkath/Galvek attempts and retries, not an assumed fixed drop count. Refill food, Prayer and enchanted bolts against the <em>remaining</em> bank after Fight Caves. For quest phases check <strong>insulated boots, axe, machete, pickaxe, chisel, lit light source, hammer, saw, 8 oak planks, 10 swamp paste and at least 12 nails plus spares; catspeak amulet (e) and ghostspeak amulet; one goutweed; one cut dragonstone, 2 molten glass, glassblowing pipe and spade; 1 astral rune; seal of passage for Lunar Isle; tinderbox, pestle and mortar; and runes for three Fire Wave casts</strong>. Bank/regear by phase; this is a whole-quest checklist, not one inventory.</p>
        <p><strong>Dragonstone fallback:</strong> search for a cut/uncut dragonstone, complete crystal key or both key halves <em>before</em> farming anything. If a key/halves exist, combine the halves if needed, open the <strong>Taverley crystal chest for its guaranteed uncut dragonstone</strong>, then cut it with the route's 70+ Crafting. If none exists, fight <strong>Goraks on the Gorak Plane via fairy ring DIR</strong> for both key halves: the main gem table lists approximately <strong>1/128 for the loop half and 1/128 for the tooth half</strong>. Bring strong defensive/crush-resistant gear, food, restore/stat-recovery supplies as needed, and fairy-ring/teleport access. Protection prayers do <em>not</em> block Gorak attacks. A ring of wealth improves the rates <em>if already owned</em>; making one now would be circular because it consumes a dragonstone. Combine the halves, open the Taverley chest for its <strong>guaranteed</strong> uncut dragonstone, cut it, and continue DS2. This is a repeatable RNG bridge for a mandatory material, <strong>not a fixed kill count or a dragonstone drop from Goraks</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Gorak" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gorak drops and combat</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_chest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guaranteed chest reward</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-ds2" number="12" title="Complete Dragon Slayer II with the retained ranged kit">
        <p>Use the <strong>adamant crossbow</strong> (RCB only if already owned), anti-dragon shield, Ava's accumulator and banked d'hide/Barrows gloves. For the quest <strong>Vorkath</strong>, pre-pot before entry—it wakes immediately in the quest—and use shield <em>plus</em> ordinary antifire for two dragonfire layers. Protect from Missiles for a ranged crossbow setup, cure poison/venom, move at once from the lobbed fireball, keep walking during acid and use <strong>Crumble Undead</strong> on the spawn (or a ranged hit if prepared). Ruby (e) is for high HP; switch to diamond (e) as HP falls. Keep enough supplies for retries, not an invented fixed bolt consumption.</p>
        <p>The fleet has checkpoints between sections; <strong>Galvek's own four-phase fight has none</strong>. Refill after a checkpoint. On Galvek, shield + antifire remain the ordinary baseline; Protect from Magic in phase 1, then Protect from Missiles for later ranged phases. Move <strong>two tiles away</strong> from the launched fireball; antifire does not stop that special. Avoid phase-1 fire traps, phase-3 tsunami through its gap, and the phase-4 binding rock; keep run energy and Auto Retaliate off. Ruby (e) helps against his large HP pool, then diamond (e) near the end (around 150 HP). Do not require Bowfa, blowpipe, dragon crossbow, crystal armour or Rigour. The lower-tier kit may take practice and multiple trips.</p>
        <p><strong>Death/retry:</strong> the DS2 dream, Vorkath and fleet/Galvek instances use deathbanks, not free Fight-Cave-style retries. Torfinn can reclaim the Vorkath/fleet items for <strong>100,000 coins</strong>; retrieve a deathbank promptly before any further unsafe death, which can erase its contents. Check Hardcore status separately. The first failure should teach a mechanic or supply adjustment, not trigger a rare-weapon hunt. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dragon_Slayer_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current fight, checkpoint and reclaim guide</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the fixed <strong>80,000 Smithing, 60,000 Mining, 50,000 Agility and 50,000 Thieving XP</strong>. Speak to <strong>Ellen in the Myths' Guild</strong> for <strong>four separate 25,000-XP combat selections</strong>, each eligible for Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic. They are post-quest dialogue rewards, not automatically spent at the quest-complete screen; claim and record all four now so deferral cannot be forgotten. With actual 75 Magic already solved, choose <strong>Strength by default</strong> unless a live combat need is clearer. Count the four rewards once. The Smithing XP reduces the later Blood Moon Rises actual-72 remainder; do not claim it completes that gate without checking live XP.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <ExpandableNote title="Recommended later upgrade: Ava's assembler" label="Optional; never Quest Cape progress">
        <p>Post-quest Vorkath can drop a head early, and the head is guaranteed by kill 50 if still dry. Bring it to Ava with the required materials to upgrade the accumulator if you <em>want</em> that permanent ranged improvement. Up to 50 extra boss kills are not part of graduation, and neither the head nor assembler is required for DT2. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Vorkath%27s_head" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Head guarantee</a>.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Only remaining DT2 skill gate</div><h2>Train the live Runecraft remainder, no farther.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-rc-60" number="13" title="Reach actual 60 Runecraft for Desert Treasure II">
        <p>The conservative Fremennik Exiles exit was <strong>196,636 Runecraft XP</strong>; actual 60 begins at <strong>273,742 XP</strong>. Thus the <em>maximum</em> untouched remainder is <strong>273,742 − 196,636 = 77,106 XP</strong>. Read the live XP now and train only <strong>max(0, 273,742 − live RC XP)</strong>. Use existing essence/pouches first. <strong>Guardians of the Rift</strong>, explained in 3.2, is the default structured loop; <strong>Ourania/ZMI</strong> is a reasonable change of pace. Stop at actual 60. No 65-RC diary grind or fixed essence mountain belongs here. <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-2/`}>3.2 Runecraft primer</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Desert Treasure II · the Fallen Empire</div><h2>Four distinct boss lanes, then the final sequence.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-dt2-preflight" number="14" title="Verify every Desert Treasure II gate and prepare modular supplies">
        <p>Check actual <strong>75 Firemaking, 75 Magic, 70 Thieving, 62 Herblore, 60 Runecraft and 60 Construction</strong>. In the journal, verify <strong>Desert Treasure I, Secrets of the North, Enakhra's Lament, Temple of the Eye, The Garden of Death, Below Ice Mountain and His Faithful Servants</strong> are green; the long Making Friends with My Arm/General's Shadow/Devious Minds/Hazeel Cult chain is already consumed by Secrets. Start at the <strong>Ancient Vault north-east of Nardah</strong> only when those checks pass.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Buy the rune deficit and recover the small tools" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Reserve the opening <strong>8 death, 16 chaos, 2 fire, 3 air, 4 water, 2 soul and 2 blood runes</strong> as one complete four-Burst set. Buy missing runes from <strong>Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle</strong>; the seal of passage is still the ordinary access item. The opening casts consume that set. Buy further Shadow-spell casts for Leviathan and the chosen boss-combat spells separately instead of reusing the opening numbers as a whole-quest budget.</p>
          <p>Reclaim the ring of visibility from <strong>Rasolo west of the Fishing Guild</strong>; buy a facemask at a Slayer equipment shop, a tinderbox from a general store and a pestle from Jatix if missing. Reuse your pickaxe. Puzzle herbs, mushrooms, salts and special quest devices are collected in their respective lanes; no outside herb batch replaces Duke's arena preparation.</p>
          <p>Refill <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions, antipoison and energy supplies</a> before each lane. If the one-time Ancient staff purchase below was already used and the staff lost, a <strong>staff of earth from Zaff in Varrock</strong> can autocast the standard-book Earth Wave baseline. The four opening Ancient spells and Leviathan's Shadow stuns can be cast manually while on Ancients; another rare staff is not a hard prerequisite.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Bring the ring of visibility, <strong>Ancient Magicks</strong> and enough runes for <strong>Blood, Ice, Smoke and Shadow Burst</strong> to open the initial route (at least 8 death, 16 chaos, 2 fire, 3 air, 4 water, 2 soul and 2 blood runes). <strong>Use Ancients whenever stunning the Leviathan with Shadow spells; switch to the standard spellbook before any Whisperer attempt using the Earth Wave baseline below.</strong> Keep a <strong>facemask from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> for the choking passages in The Scar; a Slayer helmet is not assumed. A pickaxe, tinderbox and pestle can be obtained in the quest, but carrying familiar tools may be simpler. For each boss attempt, take its one primary weapon set and small mechanic switch, a one-click exit where usable, a few Prayer restores, any relevant antipoison/energy and then fill the remaining slots with real food. Travel supplies and a modest banked rune reserve matter more than speculative upgrades. Bank and rebuild inventory between the four lanes; do not try to carry four bosses' kits at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Desert_Treasure_II_-_The_Fallen_Empire" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current prerequisites and quest phases</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-dt2" number="15" title="Complete Desert Treasure II with deterministic melee, ranged and Magic setups">
        <p><strong>Baseline:</strong> dragon scimitar or the route's situational Arkan blade, dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and normal defensive gear for melee; adamant crossbow/optional owned RCB, Ava's accumulator, banked d'hide and <em>remaining</em> plain/diamond (e) bolts for range. Use ruby (e) only where a high-HP target makes it worthwhile; the 3.3 quantities were an initial shared buffer, not a fresh refill at every boss. For Magic, the <strong>one-time 80,000-coin Ancient staff from Eblis after DT1</strong> can autocast both Ancient and standard combat spells, provided you are on the matching spellbook. It is a purchasable weapon floor, not a trident drop. Bank-check affordable runes and a magic-accuracy outfit before each attempt. No powered staff, Slayer drop or rare magic armour is universal.</p>
        <p><strong>Vardorvis — melee/slash:</strong> use dragon scimitar/defender, Protect from Melee and Piety. His auto-attacks heal him, so keep prayer up; shift around the arena's edge to miss axes and floor spikes, briefly switch to Protect from Missiles for the head projectile that disables overheads, and click away the red spores. The fight accelerates as HP drops. Re-bank before the Kasonde follow-up. <strong>Leviathan — range:</strong> stay outside bite range with the crossbow and read orb colours on impact: blue Magic, green Missiles, orange Melee. Cast a <strong>Shadow spell</strong> with the Ancient staff to stun, then attack from behind to reset the accelerating attack rhythm; run around lightning, move off falling-rock shadows and use a boulder for the smoke blast. At the final 20%, follow the moving abyssal pathfinder so prayers work and attacks gain accuracy. The Shadow cast is a mechanic, not a mandate to train Magic beyond 75.</p>
        <p><strong>Duke Sucellus — melee:</strong> collect the arena mushrooms/salt, grind and ferment the two poisons while dodging the extremities' gaze, then wake Duke. Use the slash/crush melee kit with Protect from Melee; stay near the pillar-safe side, move when a gas vent activates, and avoid the ice-spike slam. <strong>Whisperer — Magic:</strong> bring the blackstone fragment and affordable Magic-accuracy gear. The current Whisperer has a <strong>60% Earth weakness</strong>. Our reproducible damage plan is <strong>Earth Wave on the standard spellbook</strong> at the already-guaranteed 75 Magic, autocast with the purchased Ancient staff (or another owned compatible staff): each cast needs <strong>5 air, 7 earth and 1 blood rune</strong>, so budget a trial batch from the live bank. Earth Wave's 20 base max at 75 becomes a stronger ordinary hit against that weakness without any trident. Keep distance after her binding special rather than expecting a freeze. If you prefer <strong>Ancient ice spells</strong> to freeze that approach, switch to Ancients and use the same staff, accepting a slower damage lane; upgraded Iban's staff/Iban Blast is another <em>standard-book</em> fallback but does not exploit Earth weakness. Never describe Iban's spell or Earth Wave as usable while on Ancients. Pray against the incoming <strong>Magic or Ranged</strong> volleys, move after each set to avoid tentacles, activate the fragment for Shadow-Realm specials, kill a matching set of souls, step on the safe seeds and hide behind pillars for screeches. Protect sanity: the enraged ending is faster and still needs movement/prayer reads. This is a demanding mechanics fight even with the quest-version HP; do not sell the baseline as a guaranteed first try. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Whisperer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Earth weakness and fight reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Final sequence:</strong> the Mysterious Figure switches protection prayers, so bring both melee and range and dodge the post-stun purple orb. Re-bank before the four wights; the deterministic slash/crossbow pair works, but that encounter restarts from the first wight if you leave or die. Watch the Assassin's poison clouds and use the white smoke, kill Ketla clones, and follow each later wight's movement/prayer mechanic rather than trying to tank the whole room. <strong>Deaths are not free/safe:</strong> quest boss graves can be outside the arena or at the relevant re-entry point; confirm the current in-game gravestone/reclaim prompt before each retry, retrieve promptly, and budget supplies. Wilderness-like zero-risk assumptions from Fight Caves do not apply. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Desert_Treasure_II_-_The_Fallen_Empire" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full quest boss mechanics and routes</a>.</p>
        <p>After completion, claim <strong>three ancient lamps of 100,000 XP each</strong>. Eligible skills at actual 60+ are <strong>Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged, Magic and Prayer</strong>—not Slayer. Read the live combat tab. <strong>Strength is the default</strong> if it has useful room to grow; Prayer or Hitpoints may have a clearer immediate payoff, or Strength may already be far ahead. This is three distinct lamps, allocated once each, not a new required combat target. Record the <strong>Ring of shadows</strong> and <strong>Scar essence mine</strong> unlocks. Post-quest boss uniques are entirely optional.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.5 complete · guaranteed route exit</div>
        <h3>The old Grandmasters and their prerequisite chains are closed.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests:</strong> the named cleanup quests, Contact!, Beneath Cursed Sands, Enakhra's Lament, Secrets of the North, Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II complete; Curse of the Empty Lord, The General's Shadow and His Faithful Servants complete as required miniquests.</li>
          <li><strong>Skills/rewards:</strong> actual 60+ Runecraft; DS2's fixed 80k Smithing/60k Mining/50k Agility/50k Thieving claimed; Contact's one two-use combat lamp, Ellen's four 25k choices and DT2's three 100k lamps each recorded once.</li>
          <li><strong>Carry forward:</strong> Fire Cape, actual 75+ Magic/Ranged and 74+ Slayer, deterministic crossbow/melee kit, live remaining bolt/rune/cash stock, Ring of shadows and Scar essence access. Read the <em>live</em> skill tab for the final Blood Moon Rises gaps; do not assume optional XP landed.</li>
          <li><strong>Never guaranteed:</strong> RCB, Bowfa/crystal armour, blowpipe, trident, black mask/Slayer helmet, Rigour, Ava's assembler, Barrows gear or any post-quest boss unique.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
